# Konta2r optional Edge Function configuration.
# Supabase automatically provides SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_DB_URL,
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEYS, SUPABASE_SECRET_KEYS and SUPABASE_JWKS.
# Never commit a populated copy of this file.

# Node credential HMAC peppers are NOT environment variables anymore.
# They are generated inside Postgres and encrypted with Supabase Vault via
# supabase/vault.sql. The active key version defaults to 1, so this variable is
# only required when rotating to a newer Vault secret.
# KONTA2R_NODE_TOKEN_ACTIVE_KEY_VERSION=2

# Rotation procedure:
# 1. create konta2r_node_token_pepper_v2 in Vault with a fresh random value;
# 2. set KONTA2R_NODE_TOKEN_ACTIVE_KEY_VERSION=2 for the Edge Functions;
# 3. rotate live node credentials through node-lifecycle;
# 4. retire Vault v1 only after no stored credential has key_version=1.
